        "description": "Footnote*******states24gNa2S·9H2O and100mLdistilledwater,filtersterilizedandstoredunderN2; sourcecallsit1M. Preservewateraddedbasisandnominalmolaritywithoutasserting24gperfinal100mL. Receivingdoseis1.5mL; different5%andneutralizedsulfidestocksremainseparate. NBRC1257 uses 12 g Na2S·9H2O plus 50 mL distilled water; NBRC1321 uses 24 g plus 100 mL. Both give the same precursor-to-added-water ratio, call the preparation 1.0 M, specify filtration and storage under N2. This is formulation equivalence at scaled batch size, not a claim that either is made up to a final volume. MIM1167 successor removes Nitrogen as a material component while retaining source atmosphere conditions in notes/evidence.",
